can go through that sort of reliably helps them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:56.160
plan out their story right some writers consider&nbsp;
themselves very intuitive writers and they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:04.560
pantsers instead of plotters I don't think that&nbsp;
even those writers that consider themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.400
sort of intuitive writers I don't think&nbsp;
that I get a lot of pushback from them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:16.320
usually those writers if they've been through a&nbsp;
few writing projects and it's been a struggle to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.760
get all the way through because they haven't&nbsp;
had a map to kind of guide them through it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:24.320
an outline they're usually not pushing back&nbsp;
on needing an outline they're coming to me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:29.280
because they're like okay I don't really love&nbsp;
the outlining process but I feel like I need one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.680
in order to help me get through the draft right so&nbsp;
more than anything they're coming to me and saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:40.480
like I want to learn a little bit about outlining&nbsp;
that I can maybe incorporate into my more freeform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:47.440
process but that will give me some structure to&nbsp;
kind of help me get through the writing and you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:53.440
think when we tell a writer that this outlining&nbsp;
is so much part of the process and really if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:59.280
don't have one it's like building a house without&nbsp;
a good set of sort of blueprints that it's like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.920
pulling back this this magical curtain that they&nbsp;
thought it was just going to be this free-flowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:12.560
thing and it's almost disappointing in some way I&nbsp;
hope it's not disappointing but yeah I think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:18.880
maybe maybe coming up with a story in the&nbsp;
outlining process to some writers feels like it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:26.480
it's going to be too technical and too&nbsp;
rigid right but but if you actually start&nbsp;&nbsp;

