because outlining can mean so many different&nbsp;
things to so many different writers right so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:37.120
if you actually start kind of working through&nbsp;
different steps different tools different types&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:42.800
of processes to get get through an outline you'll&nbsp;
see that it's really adaptable it's the process of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:49.520
outlining is kind of whatever you make of it it's&nbsp;
whatever helps you prepare to write whatever it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:55.920
you're writing so I don't know I don't think it's&nbsp;
I don't think it's necessarily like disappointing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:01.840
to writers but I think that it's maybe eye-opening&nbsp;
like they they figure out kind of what outlining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.680
really is and and what it is is specific to&nbsp;
them it's like whatever's going to help you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.640
plan enough that you have that kind of&nbsp;
structure to get through writing your draft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:18.800
is outlining a burden or is it really part of the&nbsp;
process well I think it's part of the process for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:25.680
sure I hope that writers don't think of it as a&nbsp;
