00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:45.280
it doesn't feel like a burden I do think that&nbsp;
whatever sort of prep you do for your story is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:51.520
part of your own personal process and whether&nbsp;
you are a very detailed outliner or more of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:56.000
just a like sort of broad broad strokes I got to&nbsp;
figure out kind of the general shape of my story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:02.240
I consider all of that sort of the pre-writing&nbsp;
or outlining process so whatever it is for you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:07.840
is is part of the process for you why is it hard&nbsp;
for writers who think they have a great idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:13.440
to actually start writing their ideas down and&nbsp;
begin the writing process that's a good question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:18.640
I'm sure there are a lot of different answers to&nbsp;
this question just depending on the writer I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:24.080
part of it is probably fear right and that fear&nbsp;
can also be different for different writers too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:32.000
before you write anything down I think an idea can&nbsp;
feel complete and perfect in your head and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:38.320
when you sit down to start actually breaking it&nbsp;
down or planning it you can it can be a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.280
surprising at how little you actually know about&nbsp;
the idea before you started to try to write it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.800
down it felt very complete and perfect and then&nbsp;
when you start to write it sometimes it can or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:53.600
start to plan it can feel like oh I thought I had&nbsp;
more of this figured out or I thought this idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.600 --> 00:06:01.840
was a little bit more solid or complete so I think&nbsp;
that can be scary and can discourage people from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:08.720
beginning the process because they feel like they&nbsp;
want to figure out more of it in their head still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:14.080
before they start putting anything on paper I&nbsp;
actually think putting it on paper is kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:20.240
what helps you work through that and and helps&nbsp;
you figure out your story so I would encourage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.680
people to go ahead and just start but but yeah&nbsp;
I think it's probably fear something can feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:33.200
very solid and makes sense before you have&nbsp;
to articulate it and then when you try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:40.720
articulate it ends up sort of showing the holes in&nbsp;
it so you think it's because a lot of writers or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:45.920
quote unquote artists in general live in their&nbsp;
heads so much and and it feels so real to them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:51.200
the story and then when you actually say okay&nbsp;
let's actually see it on the and and then it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:56.160
it's you're you're about asking them to be in&nbsp;
reality yeah I'm sure that that there is truth to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:03.520
that because so many writers are living in their&nbsp;
imaginations a lot of the time I also think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:09.120
a lot of times when we get inspired by a story&nbsp;
idea we get really excited about it what we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:14.720
thinking about most of the time is that sort&nbsp;
of act one setup portion of it it's like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:20.320
